Full Stack 3D Viewer Implementation Plan
Implement a 3D viewer with upload capabilities and persistent settings.

Proposed Changes
Backend (Node.js + Express)
[NEW] 
BACKEND/middleware/upload.js
Configure multer to store files in uploads/ directory.
Filter for .glb and 
.gltf
 files.
[NEW] 
BACKEND/models/Settings.js
Schema: backgroundColor (String), wireframe (Boolean), timestamp (Date).
[MODIFY] 
BACKEND/index.js
Serve uploads folder statically.
Add routes:
POST /api/upload: Handle file upload, return URL.
POST /api/settings: Save viewer settings.
GET /api/settings: Get latest settings.
Frontend (React)
[MODIFY] 
FRONTEND/src/App.jsx
State Management: Add state for modelUrl, bgColor, isWireframe.
Three.js Update:
Import OrbitControls.
Update scene background dynamically based on state.
Traverse scene to update material wireframe property based on state.
Load model from modelUrl state instead of hardcoded path.
UI Components:
Add <input type="file"> for upload.
Add <input type="color"> for background.
Add <button> or checkbox for wireframe toggle.
Add "Save Settings" button.
API Integration:
handleUpload: POST file to backend, update modelUrl.
saveSettings: POST state to backend.
useEffect: Fetch settings on mount.
Verification Plan
Automated Tests
None.
Manual Verification
Upload: Upload a local .glb file. Verify it appears in the viewer.
Controls: Test Rotate, Zoom, Pan.
Customization: Change background color and toggle wireframe. Verify visual changes.
Persistence: Click "Save Settings". Refresh page. Verify settings (color, wireframe) are restored.